# Wave W17-X (Route 212 — North): pool willow — a pool willow in deep bog greens: a broad low crown that droops, its strands hanging long past the crown’s edge toward the pools it shades, pale pool-glints struck through the strands, highlight lifted to the crown’s top, on pool turf (ground baked in). Route 212 — North’s own tree — split from Maris’s fordwillow by register entire (bog pools vs river ford: this willow is darker, its strands longer, its water still) and from Route 212 — South’s bog pine by posture: the willow leans to the pools, the pine stands out of them.
